<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mali</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mali refers both to the medieval <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mali-empire">Mali Empire</a> and to the region of the upper and middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>, now the Republic of Mali. The area was a centre of trans-Saharan trade in gold and salt. It was successively dominated by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>, Mali and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai</a> empires, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mandinka">Mandinka</a> heartland of Mali also gave rise to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaabu-empire">Kaabu Empire</a> to the west.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mali.jpg" alt="Mali" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SKopp · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Mali.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
